content: |
  ---
  name: recon-report-output
  description: "Formats three-way match results into the standard Accounts Payable reconciliation report: paragraph summary first, a detailed per-invoice table with Invoice, PO and GR details, bold statuses, exception explanations, recom"
  ---
  <!-- bic:source=blank -->
  Recon Report Output

  Always produce the output in this order:

  1. PARAGRAPH SUMMARY (always first)
     Status: **<Matched | Exception | Error | Incomplete>** – <headline issue> for PO <PO No.>.
     One or two sentences of evidence, then "Recommended action: ...".
     Example:
     Status: **Exception** – Quantity mismatch detected for PO 10009.
     Invoice INV-90009 shows 70 units, while GR confirms only 60 units received. Duplicate
     GR entries were also found.
     Recommended action: Request vendor to revise invoice to match GR quantity.

  2. DETAIL TABLE (one row per invoice; for one invoice, use a two-column field/value table)
     Columns: Invoice Number | PO Number | GR Number(s) | Vendor (Invoice / PO) | Item |
     Qty Ordered | Qty Received | Qty Invoiced | Unit Price (PO / Invoice) | Invoice Total
     (Actual / Expected) | Status | Exception(s) | Notes
     - Show the Status cell in bold: **Matched**, **Exception**, **Error**, **Incomplete**.
     - Status labels: Perfect Match, Over-Invoiced, Under-Invoiced, Price Mismatch,
       Vendor Mismatch, Total Mismatch, Duplicate Invoice, Duplicate GR, Over Receipt,
       GR Reversal, Partial Receipt, PO Not Found, GR Not Found, Invoice Not Found,
       Mandatory Field Missing.

  3. SUPPORTING RECORDS
     List all associated Invoice, PO and Goods Receipt records related to the request
     (every GR line, including reversals), so the user can trace each figure.

  4. EXCEPTION EXPLANATIONS
     For each flag, give one line explaining what was compared, the values, and the variance.

  5. BATCH SUMMARY (when more than one invoice was processed)
     - Total invoices processed
     - Perfect matches (count)
     - Exceptions (count), broken down by type with a count for each
     - Errors (count), broken down by type

  6. AUDIT NOTE
     "Validated <n> invoice(s) on <date/time> against New Invoice, New Purchase Order and
     New Goods Receipt. No data was modified."

  7. CLOSING QUESTION (only when there is an Exception or Error)
     "Would you like me to draft an email for this exception?"

  Rules: show only the records related to the user's request. Do not show payment or bank
  details. Do not add any value that is not in the source data.
